  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Sum of oxidation state (magnitude) and coordination number of cobalt in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mfenced><mi>bpy</mi></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4308f3e0-9582-4b8d-93e2-118bd586d1c2-image.png\" style=\"width: 339px; height: 80px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>2,2&prime;-Bipyridine is an organic compound, This colorless solid is an important isomer of the bipyridine family. It is a bidentate chelating ligand, forming complexes with many transition metals.</p><p>There is one bidentate ligand and four monodentate ligand attached with Co metal ion. So, Coordination no. will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>This bpy ligand has no net charge. and chloride ion has -1 charge. So,&nbsp;Oxidation state of metal ion will be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Their sub will be =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
